  "print": "bird",
  "_about": "ALLOSAURUS FRAGILIS (sculpt overlay, 2026-11-05, after Hartman's and Paul's skeletals): 8.5 m, the hips 2.15 m up, the body level and the tail held out level; an S-curved neck lifting the head to 3 m; a long, narrow 0.85 m skull with small triangular lacrimal horns in front of the eyes and a low paired ridge along the nasals; strong three-fingered arms (the forearm a little shorter than the humerus) with big curved claws, the thumb's the biggest; long legs, three toes. Ochre-tan with a darker brown back, faint bands, a cream belly; the horns rufous. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur. (2026-11-08, review.py: hand claws) The HAND: each finger one smooth horn (faired into the hand, a rounded fingertip) instead of a field cone and a six-sided tube that came out as blocky shards on the coarse grid round the claws' roots; the claws come out of the fingertips, 0.72 of their girth, along their old hooks (no fillet). (2026-11-08, review.py: fingers) The FINGERS (review.py knuckle_fingers): slimmer, two knuckles swelling along each, the arm's scales on them, each running into its claw -- the claw's base nearly the fingertip's girth and round, a sheath the finger ends in (they read as smooth sausages with a thin claw poking out).",
